          dealing: 'All cards are dealt out evenly to the players face-down. Players may not look at their cards.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid being the last player to slap the pile (or be the first, depending on variant) and capture all cards to win.',
          gameplay: "1. Players take turns flipping one card face-up onto a central pile in a rhythmic fashion.\n2. **The Chant**: As each card is played, the current player says a rank in ascending order: 'Seven', 'Eight', 'Nine', 'Ten', 'Jack', 'Queen', 'King', 'Ace', then repeats.\n3. **The Kloepper (Knock)**: If the card revealed matches the rank being spoken, all players must immediately slap their hand onto the central pile.\n4. **Penalty**: The last player to slap takes the entire pile of cards and adds it to their personal stack.\n5. **Fake-Outs**: If a player slaps the pile when no match has occurred, they take the pile as a penalty.",
          keyRules: [
            'Players chant ranks in ascending order',
            'Slap when card matches the spoken rank',
            'Last to slap takes the pile',
            'False slaps result in penalty',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Maintain the rhythm. If you lose the beat of the chant, you will be late to react when the match occurs. Focus on the dealer's hand movement.",
          intermediate: "Peripheral Vision: Don't stare at the center. Watch the player whose turn it is next. If you see them flinching to slap, you should slap too.",
          advanced: "Rhythmic Deception: Some high-level variants allow the current player to pause slightly or speed up their flip to bait opponents into a 'fake' slap (foul).",
          tips: [
            'Keep your slapping hand close to the table edge, not in your lap.',
            "In drinking variants, the person who takes the pile also 'takes a sip'.",
            'Pay attention when the chant resets from Ace back to Seven; this is the most common moment for reaction errors.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
